# The build context for `docker/lsp.Dockerfile`, which needs the *source* and
# nothing built.
#
# `just lsp-docker` bind-mounts the repository at run time, so this context is
# only what `docker build` sends — but an unfiltered context here would ship a
# multi-gigabyte `target/` to the daemon on every build, and the tracked capture
# library on top of it. Both are pure cost: neither is read by the image.

# Build output, host-shaped. `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` in the image points elsewhere
# precisely so the two never meet.
target/
**/target/

# The Tier-2 capture library — PNGs and GIFs, tracked, and irrelevant to a
# language server.
tapes/artifacts/

# Worktrees. `.claude/worktrees/` holds whole checkouts, so leaving this out is
# the difference between a small context and a recursive one.
.claude/

# Git's own object store. The image needs no history.
.git/
